E\u00a0\u00a0FIRED!", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToPbNSke", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 11, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "stable", "id": 8904854, "raw_content": "Like any Product one is trying to sell, \"New and Improved\" has a specific rhetorical structure: it implies a change without specifying one. The consumer is meant to feel that something got better, but the \"what\" is deliberately vague. The packaging changed, the formula maybe didn't, the \"improvement\" is a claim, not a measurement.\n\n\"Democracy\" in the regime-naming context works identically. They don't say \"we are a new and improved Democracy compared to the Republic\" \u2014 they just said \"we are a Democracy.\" The \"improvement\" is baked into the word itself, unexamined. Same with \"People's Republic\" or \"Democratic Republic\" or \"Socialist Republic\"\u2014 the adjective is doing all the work. It's a brand claim, not a specification.\n\nMore bags and boxes of the same shit labelled with the claim 'People's Choice'...\n\n\n\n", "author": "Moebius", "created": 1792950857927, "profile_picture": "0F9hm63l5dUw", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Moebius", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Communist DSA's 'New and Improved 'Democracy'...More Socialist Political Rhetoric -- Just Like All Political Rhetoric...", "last_comment_created": 1792953261278, "content": "<p>Like any Product one is trying to sell, &quot;New and Improved&quot; has a specific rhetorical structure: it implies a change without specifying one. The consumer is meant to feel that something got better, but the &quot;what&quot; is deliberately vague. The packaging changed, the formula maybe didn't, the &quot;improvement&quot; is a claim, not a measurement.</p>\n<p>&quot;Democracy&quot; in the regime-naming context works identically. They don't say &quot;we are a new and improved Democracy compared to the Republic&quot; \u2014 they just said &quot;we are a Democracy.&quot; The &quot;improvement&quot; is baked into the word itself, unexamined. Same with &quot;People's Republic&quot; or &quot;Democratic Republic&quot; or &quot;Socialist Republic&quot;\u2014 the adjective is doing all the work. It's a brand claim, not a specification.</p>\n<p>More bags and boxes of the same shit labelled with the claim 'People's Choice'...</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 11, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "\ud83d\uded1\u00a0\u00a0Corrupt Commies\u00a0\u00a0\ud83d\uded1", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToPbMds9", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 20, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8904599, "raw_content": "Secret Mega-Alliance Exposed as DataRepublican Keeps Dropping More \u2018Democracy Files\u2019...Recordings describe red-line scenarios, transitional governance proposals, and coordination involving federal workers and a secretive alliance of NGOs\n\nhttps://www.lifezette.com/2026/10/secret-mega-alliance-exposed-as-datarepublican-keeps-dropping-more-democracy-files-watch/\n\n", "author": "ashlanddog", "created": 1792939056914, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "FreedomLubber", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": 